      "content": "That's a pretty intense stance. You're saying the government basically loses its right to rule if it uses these tools. But isn't that a bit extreme? Most people would say it's a trade-off—we give up a little privacy so we can actually live in a safe society. Isn't that just the reality of a modern social contract?",
